<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paestum</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Paistom</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paestum is an ancient city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, founded as the Greek colony of Poseidonia around 600 BCE. Taken by the Lucanians around 410 BCE and refounded as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> colony in 273 BCE, it is renowned for three well-preserved Doric temples and the painted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomb-of-the-diver">Tomb of the Diver</a>. It is part of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paestum.jpg" alt="Paestum" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oliver-Bonjoch · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Veduta_di_Paestum_2010.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
